# Workflow Example: Decision Lifecycle

Purpose:
  Immutable example showing how a decision flows through the SDDRA system.
  This example demonstrates the decision lifecycle from proposal to closure.

Example Decision: DEC-100
Title: "Use PostgreSQL for payment transactions"

Lifecycle:

  1. PROPOSED
     Who: AI
     When: During D1 stage, after analyzing requirements
     Input: docs/30-backend/overview.md
     Output: DEC-100.sdd (proposed)
     Token: in=500, out=200, delta=300
     State: ~

  2. REVIEW
     Who: Human
     When: After D1 stage, before S1
     Input: DEC-100.sdd + docs/
     Output: review feedback
     Token: in=200, out=100, delta=100
     Gate: human_required
     State: @

  3. APPROVED
     Who: Human
     When: After review
     Input: review feedback
     Output: DEC-100.sdd (approved)
     Token: in=100, out=50, delta=50
     Gate: human_required
     State: +

  4. IMPLEMENTED
     Who: AI
     When: During C1 stage
     Input: .sdd/project/ + DEC-100.sdd
     Output: project/backend/payment/repository.go
     Token: in=5000, out=15000, delta=10000
     State: >

  5. VERIFIED
     Who: QA
     When: During QA stage
     Input: project/backend/payment/repository.go + tests
     Output: test results
     Token: in=15000, out=2000, delta=13000
     State: *

  6. CLOSED
     Who: Human
     When: After verification
     Input: test results + verification report
     Output: DEC-100.sdd (closed)
     Token: in=2000, out=100, delta=1900
     State: _

Decision Record:
  ID: DEC-100
  Type: technical
  Status: closed
  Title: Use PostgreSQL for payment transactions
  Context: Payment module requires ACID compliance
  Problem: Need database with strong consistency
  Options:
    1. PostgreSQL — Pros: ACID, JSON support; Cons: heavier than Redis
    2. Redis — Pros: fast; Cons: eventual consistency
    3. MySQL — Pros: mature; Cons: less JSON support
  Decision: PostgreSQL
  Rationale: ACID compliance required for financial transactions
  Impact:
    Files: [project/backend/payment/repository.go]
    Modules: [payment]
    Risks: [R1]
  Owner: human
  Reviewers: [backend, database]
  Approved_By: human
  Approved_At: 2026-08-27T20:00:00Z
  Implementation:
    Tasks: [TASK-201]
    Chain: default
    Status: completed
  Verification:
    Criteria: [integration tests pass, load test > 1000 TPS]
    Status: passed
  Supersedes: null
  Conflicts: null
  Depends_On: null
  Created_At: 2026-08-27T18:00:00Z
  Updated_At: 2026-08-27T20:30:00Z

State: +
